guide forever/reputation/brood-of-nozdormu
title Brood of Nozdormu Reputation
category Reputation
folder Reputation · Raids and dungeons
levels 60-60
zone Silithus
keywords Brood of Nozdormu, Bronze Dragonflight, Anachronos, Caverns of Time, Baristolth, Scepter of the Shifting Sands, Silithid Carapace Fragment, Hand of the Righteous, Signet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight, Path of the Protector, Path of the Conqueror, Path of the Invoker, Ahn'Qiraj, Ancient Qiraji Artifact, Qiraji Lord's Insignia, Mortal Champions, Secrets of the Qiraji, Andorgos, Kandrostrasz, Narain Soothfancy, Scarab Gong
why The Bronze Dragonflight's ring, upgraded at every standing; a long climb from Hated, mostly in raids.
reward item 21200 21205 21210
reward text The Scepter of the Shifting Sands quest chain

# Built from Forever's data: the Brood of Nozdormu quest rows (reputation from Forever's quest pages; the world
# database's standing gates: The Hand of the Righteous only below Neutral, Anachronos and the whole Scepter
# chain from Neutral, the ring quests from Neutral to Revered), the kill reputation and the standing each kill
# stops at (world database), the drop tables (Silithid Carapace Fragments: one to three from every hive
# silithid of Hive'Ashi, Hive'Zora and Hive'Regal), and the client's faction table (the Brood starts at Hated 0 of 36,000: Neutral is 42,000
# away). Secrets of the Qiraji (+1,000) and Mortal Champions (+500 Brood, +100 Cenarion Circle) pay through
# spells (Forever's client spell data), so Forever's quest pages show no reputation for them.
# Forever's quest pages give several Scepter chain quests 200 where Classic paid 500 (Return to Narain, The
# Wrath of Neptulon, The Nightmare Manifests, The Might of Kalimdor, Bang a Gong!, Treasure of the Timeless One)
# and 100 where Classic paid 250 (A Pawn on the Eternal Board, The Champion Returns, the ring quests). This
# guide uses Forever's numbers. No race gets a reputation bonus in Forever; the Legacy perk Diplomat adds up
# to 10%. Numbers below are without it.
# Raids: Blackwing Lair and the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj are 40-player raids, the Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj a 20-player one.
# Instance entrances are placed from the client's map table (the corpse point outside each).
# INGAME: Are Blackwing Lair and the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj open? Blizzard's raid announcement for Forever names
# Barrow Deeps, Hyjal Summit and Onyxia's Lair; Blackwing Lair, the Temple and the Ruins are in the client but
# not announced. Without Blackwing Lair the Broodlord's head, and with it every Brood quest after the first (the
# fragment turn-ins too), is out of reach.
# INGAME: Can the Scarab Gong be rung on a Forever realm? In Classic the first scepter opens the gates for the
# whole realm once, after the war effort.
# INGAME: Do the Twin Emperors stop paying at 2,999 of 3,000 Neutral like the Temple trash? Forever's world
# database says so; Classic players reported them paying past it.

step Baristolth in Cenarion Hold
  tip The Brood of Nozdormu is not in your reputation list until you meet Anachronos. Baristolth of the Shifting Sands, in the main building of Cenarion Hold, sends you to him. Meeting him sets you at Hated, 0 of 36,000: Neutral is 42,000 reputation away, and almost all of it comes from raids. Blackwing Lair and the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj are not among the first raids Blizzard has announced for Forever: until one of them opens, the 100 from Baristolth's first quest is all the Brood reputation there is. The Legacy perk Diplomat adds up to 10% to every gain; the numbers in this guide are without it.
  getfp "Cenarion Hold"
  accept 8286                         -- Baristolth of the Shifting Sands

step Anachronos at the Caverns of Time
  zone Tanaris
  tip Anachronos, a bronze dragon in elf form, stands at the mouth of the Caverns of Time in eastern Tanaris, south-east of Gadgetzan. Walk up to him.
  complete 8286 @65.3,50.0            -- Meet Anachronos

step Back to Baristolth
  zone Silithus
  tip Only One May Rise wants the head of Broodlord Lashlayer, the third boss of Blackwing Lair (a 40-player raid in Blackrock Mountain). Everything after it needs the head, the fragment turn-ins included: until you have it, What Tomorrow Brings is all the Brood reputation there is, solo or not.
  turnin 8286                         -- 100
  accept 8288 optional

step Broodlord Lashlayer
  zone Burning Steppes
  tip Blackwing Lair is a 40-player raid at the top of Blackrock Mountain. Broodlord Lashlayer always drops his head.
  collect 20383 quest 8288.1 optional @32.5,32.4 -- Head of the Broodlord Lashlayer: raid of 40

step The Path of the Righteous
  zone Silithus
  tip The Path of the Righteous wants 200 Silithid Carapace Fragments. Every hive silithid drops one to three on most kills: the Hive'Ashi Workers, Stingers, Swarmers and Defenders north and north-west of Cenarion Hold, and those of Hive'Zora in the west and Hive'Regal in the south. Almost all of them are elites of level 57 to 60: one at a time solo, faster in a group.
  turnin 8288 optional                -- 200
  accept 8301 optional
  collect 20384 x200 quest 8301.1 optional -- Silithid Carapace Fragment
  turnin 8301 optional                -- 200

step Hated to Neutral
  tip After The Path, Baristolth takes 200 more fragments for The Hand of the Righteous: 200 reputation, again and again, but only until Neutral. From Hated 500 that is 208 turn-ins, 41,600 fragments, 20,000 to 30,000 elite kills: the only way without the Temple, and a very long one. With the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj open (a 40-player raid) it is far quicker: every Temple trash mob gives 100 until 2,999 of 3,000 Neutral, about 9,500 a full clear, so four to five clears reach Neutral. Save every Ancient Qiraji Artifact and Qiraji Lord's Insignia you loot until the trash stops counting: they pay the same later.
  collect 20384 x200 optional         -- Silithid Carapace Fragment
  turnin 8302 direct optional         -- The Hand of the Righteous: 200 fragments, 200
  rep 910 Neutral

step Anachronos's quests
  tip Neutral opens the rest of the Scepter of the Shifting Sands chain. Baristolth sends you back to Anachronos.
  accept 8303                         -- Baristolth of the Shifting Sands

step Long Forgotten Memories
  zone Tanaris
  turnin 8303                         -- Anachronos: 200
  accept 8305

step The Crystalline Tear
  zone Silithus
  tip The Crystalline Tear is a small red crystal on the ground just outside the gates of Ahn'Qiraj, in the far south-west of Silithus. Click it, then stay and watch the vision of the War of the Shifting Sands to its end. If it is cut short, abandon the quest and click the Tear again.
  turnin 8305                         -- Crystalline Tear: 50
  accept 8519
  complete 8519 @28.7,89.1            -- Watch the vision

step The Charge of the Dragonflights
  zone Tanaris
  tip Anachronos now offers the Signet Ring of the Bronze Dragonflight in three kinds: the Path of the Protector (tanks), of the Conqueror (melee fighters) or of the Invoker (casters). Take one: the other two close. Each standing from Friendly to Exalted brings an upgrade of the same ring, 100 reputation each. The Charge of the Dragonflights sends you after the three shards of the Scepter of the Shifting Sands.
  turnin 8519                         -- 100
  accept 8555
  turnin 8555                         -- 10
  talk 15192 optional                 -- Pick one: The Path of the Protector, the Conqueror or the Invoker, 100

step The red shard: Vaelastrasz
  zone Burning Steppes
  tip The red shard: Vaelastrasz the Corrupt, the second boss of Blackwing Lair, gives Nefarius's Corruption before his fight; Nefarian, the last boss, drops the Red Scepter Shard for one raider on the quest each kill. The quest lasts five hours.
  accept 8730 optional @32.5,32.4     -- Vaelastrasz the Corrupt, Blackwing Lair: raid of 40
  collect 21138 quest 8730.1 optional @32.5,32.4 -- Red Scepter Shard, Nefarian

step The blue shard: Azuregos's ledger
  zone Azshara
  tip The Spirit of Azuregos stands on the south coast of Azshara. His ledger starts Narain Soothfancy's long chain in Tanaris.
  accept 8575 optional                -- Spirit of Azuregos

step Narain Soothfancy
  zone Tanaris
  tip Narain Soothfancy, a goblin seer, lives in a hut north-east of Gadgetzan. He sends you three ways at once: to Stewvul's crate in Silverpine Forest, to an island off the south coast of Tanaris, and to Dirge Quikcleave in Gadgetzan.
  turnin 8575 optional                -- 10
  accept 8576 optional
  turnin 8576 optional                -- 10
  accept 8577 optional
  accept 8597 optional
  accept 8584 optional

step Stewvul's crate
  zone Silverpine Forest
  tip The Inconspicuous Crate leans on the Greymane Wall at the south end of Silverpine Forest, left of the closed gate.
  turnin 8577 optional                -- Inconspicuous Crate: 10
  accept 8578 optional
  collect 20951 quest 8578.1 optional @46.2,86.7 -- Narain's Scrying Goggles

step Meridith the Mermaiden
  zone Tanaris
  tip The Freshly Dug Dirt lies on the farther of two islands south of Land's End Beach, past the fatigue line. Meridith the Mermaiden, on the sea floor south of the beach's crashed gyrocopter, gives Love Song for Narain and a three-minute swim-speed blessing that gets you across.
  accept 8599 optional                -- Meridith the Mermaiden

step The island off Land's End Beach
  zone map 947
  turnin 8597 optional                -- Freshly Dug Dirt: 10
  accept 8598 optional

step Back to Narain
  zone Tanaris
  tip Decoy! sends you, disguised with Narain's turban, to a drop-off point south of Everlook in Winterspring. Leave the bag of gold there: Number Two, a level 61 elite, comes for it (group of 3 to 5).
  turnin 8578 optional                -- 10
  turnin 8598 optional                -- 10
  turnin 8599 optional                -- 10
  accept 8606 optional

step Decoy!
  zone Winterspring
  kill 15554 quest 8606.1 optional    -- Number Two, elite: group of 3 to 5

step Dirge Quikcleave
  zone Tanaris
  tip Dirge Quikcleave cooks in Gadgetzan. He sends you to the Isle of Dread off southern Feralas for a Chimaerok feast.
  turnin 8606 optional                -- Narain Soothfancy: 25
  accept 8620 optional
  turnin 8584 optional                -- Dirge Quikcleave
  accept 8585 optional

step The Isle of Dread
  zone Feralas
  tip Lord Lakmaeran and the Chimaerok on the Isle of Dread are elites of level 60 to 62 that respawn every ten minutes: a raid's work. The Chimaerok drop a tenderloin about half the time, Lakmaeran two to four now and then.
  collect 21027 quest 8585.1 optional @29.3,72.6 -- Lakmaeran's Carcass, Lord Lakmaeran: raid
  collect 21024 x20 quest 8585.2 optional @29.5,78.0 -- Chimaerok Tenderloin

step Draconic for Dummies, Volume II
  zone Dustwallow Marsh
  tip The Only Prescription needs the eight chapters of Draconic for Dummies, Volume II: from Doctor Weavil in his house on Alcaz Island (a level 63 elite with guards, raid), the Felguard Elites, Doomguard Commanders and Dreadlords of the Blasted Lands, the Hederine south of Everlook, and a book in the Undercity. Narain hands out the binding when you accept.
  collect 21111 quest 8620.1 optional @77.9,17.1 -- Draconic for Dummies: Volume II

step Dirge's Chops
  zone Tanaris
  tip Dirge wants 20 Goblin Rocket Fuel and 20 Deeprock Salt with the meat. Narain then wants 20 Arcanite Bars, 10 Elementium Ore, 10 Azerothian Diamonds and 10 Blue Sapphires, and gives you an Arcanite Buoy: placed at the Swirling Maelstrom in Azshara's Bay of Storms, it calls up Maws, a level 63 boss for a raid. Maws drops the Blue Scepter Shard for one raider on the quest each kill.
  turnin 8585 optional                -- Dirge Quikcleave
  accept 8586 optional
  collect 9061 x20 quest 8586.1 optional -- Goblin Rocket Fuel
  collect 8150 x20 quest 8586.2 optional -- Deeprock Salt
  turnin 8586 optional
  accept 8587 optional
  turnin 8587 optional                -- Narain Soothfancy: 200
  turnin 8620 optional                -- 75
  accept 8728 optional
  collect 12360 x20 quest 8728.1 optional @52.0,29.7 -- Arcanite Bar: Alchemists, or the auction house
  collect 18562 x10 quest 8728.2 optional @52.0,29.7 -- Elementium Ore: Blackwing Lair, or the auction house
  collect 12800 x10 quest 8728.3 optional -- Azerothian Diamond
  collect 12361 x10 quest 8728.4 optional -- Blue Sapphire
  turnin 8728 optional                -- 100
  accept 8729 optional

step Maws
  zone Azshara
  collect 21137 quest 8729.1 optional @68.0,52.5 -- Blue Scepter Shard, Maws: raid

step The green shard: Eranikus
  zone Swamp of Sorrows
  tip Malfurion Stormrage appears beside the Shade of Eranikus at the bottom of the Temple of Atal'Hakkar (a five-player dungeon). He sends you to a Forest Wisp outside Darnassus (Horde players walk past the city's guards), then to Keeper Remulos in Moonglade.
  accept 8733 optional @69.9,53.6     -- Malfurion Stormrage, inside the Temple of Atal'Hakkar

step The Forest Wisp
  zone Teldrassil
  turnin 8733 optional                -- Forest Wisp: 25 (and 25 Cenarion Circle)
  accept 8734 optional

step Keeper Remulos
  zone Moonglade
  tip The Nightmare's Corruption wants a fragment from each of the four Dragons of Nightmare portals: elite dragonkin at the Ashenvale, Feralas and Hinterlands portals (5% each) and the Twilight Corrupter in Duskwood. Raid content.
  turnin 8734 optional                -- 10 (and 100 Cenarion Circle)
  accept 8735 optional

step The Ashenvale portal
  zone Ashenvale
  tip The four dream portals sit in groves guarded by elite dragonkin of level 60 to 62 that respawn every 30 minutes; each drops the portal's fragment one time in twenty. Raid content.
  collect 21147 quest 8735.1 optional -- Fragment of the Nightmare's Corruption

step The Duskwood portal
  zone Duskwood
  tip The Twilight Corrupter (level 63 boss) always drops its fragment.
  collect 21149 quest 8735.2 optional -- Twilight Corrupter

step The Feralas portal
  zone Feralas
  collect 21148 quest 8735.3 optional -- Fragment of the Nightmare's Corruption

step The Hinterlands portal
  zone The Hinterlands
  collect 21146 quest 8735.4 optional -- Fragment of the Nightmare's Corruption

step The Nightmare Manifests
  zone Moonglade
  tip A raid event: follow Keeper Remulos toward Nighthaven and keep him alive against Eranikus and his nightmare adds until Tyrande arrives and redeems Eranikus. Do not kill Eranikus.
  turnin 8735 optional                -- 100 (and 100 Cenarion Circle)
  accept 8736 optional
  complete 8736 optional @36.2,41.8   -- The Redemption of Eranikus: raid
  turnin 8736 optional                -- 200 (and 200 Cenarion Circle)
  accept 8741 optional

step The Scepter of the Shifting Sands
  zone Tanaris
  tip With the three shards, Anachronos makes the Scepter of the Shifting Sands. In Classic its first holder rings the Scarab Gong once for the whole realm, opening the gates of Ahn'Qiraj, and those who finish within ten hours earn the black qiraji crystal mount; whether Forever's realms get that event is not known.
  turnin 8730 optional                -- Red Scepter Shard: 200
  turnin 8729 optional                -- Blue Scepter Shard: 200
  turnin 8741 optional                -- Green Scepter Shard: 100
  accept 8742 optional
  turnin 8742 optional                -- 200 (and 200 Cenarion Circle)

step The Scarab Gong
  zone Silithus
  tip The Scarab Gong hangs before the gates of Ahn'Qiraj. Jonathan the Revelator appears beside it once the gong has been rung, with Treasure of the Timeless One: a weapon and 200 reputation.
  accept 8743 optional                -- The Scarab Gong
  turnin 8743 optional                -- 200 (and 200 Cenarion Circle)
  accept 8745 optional                -- Jonathan the Revelator
  turnin 8745 optional                -- 200

step Neutral to Friendly in the Temple
  zone Silithus
  tip Neutral to Friendly is 3,000 reputation. Every trash mob of the Temple of Ahn'Qiraj (a 40-player raid behind the Scarab Wall) gives 100, and the Twin Emperors 210 each, until 2,999 of 3,000 Neutral, one point short of Friendly; there they stop. Then hand in one saved Ancient Qiraji Artifact (1,000, to Andorgos) or Qiraji Lord's Insignia (500, to Kandrostrasz) to tip you over. The shoulder and boot exchanges of the Temple's tier set need no standing: the token, two idols and ten scarabs to Andorgos (shoulders) or Kandrostrasz (boots) pay 200 each. The Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj (20 players) give a little from bosses: Kurinnaxx, Moam, Buru and Ayamiss 50 each, Rajaxx 34, Ossirian 100, to Exalted.
  accept 8784 optional item 21230 @29.0,92.8 -- Ancient Qiraji Artifact
  turnin 8784 optional @29.0,92.8     -- Andorgos: 1,000
  accept 8579 optional @29.0,92.8     -- Kandrostrasz
  collect 21229 quest 8579.1 optional @29.0,92.8 -- Qiraji Lord's Insignia, Temple bosses
  turnin 8579 optional @29.0,92.8     -- 500
  rep 910 Friendly

step The ring at Friendly
  zone Tanaris
  tip At Friendly, Anachronos upgrades the ring of the path you chose: The Path of the Protector, Conqueror or Invoker. Bring the ring you wear; 100 reputation.
  talk 15192 optional                 -- Anachronos: the Friendly ring quest of your path

step Friendly to Honored: the turn-ins
  zone Silithus
  tip Now hand in what you saved. Each Ancient Qiraji Artifact (any Temple trash, 1% to 9%) starts Secrets of the Qiraji: 1,000 reputation from Andorgos, one of the three bronze dragons inside the Temple. Each Qiraji Lord's Insignia (nearly every Temple boss) goes to Kandrostrasz for Mortal Champions: 500 here and 100 Cenarion Circle. C'Thun gives 2,500, to Exalted. Friendly to Honored is 6,000: six artifacts or twelve insignias. Friendly also opens the helm and leg exchanges of the Temple's tier set (200 reputation each) at Andorgos and Kandrostrasz.
  collect 21230 optional @29.0,92.8   -- Ancient Qiraji Artifact: right-click it, then Andorgos
  collect 21229 optional @29.0,92.8   -- Qiraji Lord's Insignia
  turnin 8595 direct optional @29.0,92.8 -- Mortal Champions: 1 insignia, 500
  rep 910 Honored

step The ring at Honored
  zone Tanaris
  tip At Honored, Anachronos upgrades the ring of the path you chose: The Path of the Protector, Conqueror or Invoker. Bring the ring you wear; 100 reputation.
  talk 15192 optional                 -- Anachronos: the Honored ring quest of your path

step Honored to Revered
  zone Silithus
  tip Honored to Revered is 12,000: twelve artifacts, 24 insignias, or a mix with C'Thun (2,500). After the first, each insignia is the repeatable Mortal Champions. Every Temple boss sometimes drops an Imperial Qiraji Armaments or Regalia (about one time in twenty): Arygos and Merithra of the Dream, inside the Temple once C'Thun is dead, take it with 3 Elementium Ore for 200 and a weapon. Honored opens the chest exchange of the tier set (200).
  collect 21229 optional @29.0,92.8   -- Qiraji Lord's Insignia
  turnin 8595 direct optional @29.0,92.8 -- Mortal Champions: 1 insignia, 500
  collect 21232 optional @29.0,92.8   -- Imperial Qiraji Armaments
  collect 21237 optional @29.0,92.8   -- Imperial Qiraji Regalia
  collect 18562 x3 optional @32.5,32.4 map 1428 -- Elementium Ore, Blackwing Lair or the auction house
  turnin 8789 direct optional @29.0,92.8 -- Arygos: Armaments and 3 Elementium Ore, 200
  turnin 8790 direct optional @29.0,92.8 -- Merithra of the Dream: Regalia and 3 Elementium Ore, 200
  rep 910 Revered

step The ring at Revered
  zone Tanaris
  tip At Revered, Anachronos upgrades the ring of the path you chose: The Path of the Protector, Conqueror or Invoker. Bring the ring you wear; 100 reputation.
  talk 15192 optional                 -- Anachronos: the Revered ring quest of your path

step Revered to Exalted
  zone Silithus
  tip Revered to Exalted is 21,000: 21 artifacts or 42 insignias, with C'Thun's 2,500 a week. C'Thun's eye starts C'Thun's Legacy for Caelestrasz (200, and 200 Cenarion Circle). At Exalted Anachronos gives the last ring: The Protector of Kalimdor, The Qiraji Conqueror or The Grand Invoker.
  collect 21229 optional @29.0,92.8   -- Qiraji Lord's Insignia
  turnin 8595 direct optional @29.0,92.8 -- Mortal Champions: 1 insignia, 500
  accept 8801 optional item 21221 @29.0,92.8 -- Eye of C'Thun
  turnin 8801 optional @29.0,92.8     -- Caelestrasz: 200
  rep 910 Exalted

step The Exalted ring
  zone Tanaris
  tip At Exalted, Anachronos gives the last ring of your path: The Protector of Kalimdor, The Qiraji Conqueror or The Grand Invoker. Bring the Revered ring; 100 reputation.
  talk 15192 optional                 -- Anachronos: the Exalted ring quest of your path
